, and now we may not)Tj T* (touch them \(Joshua 9:19\). The Gibeonites were spared and)Tj T* (became woodcutters and water carriers for the house of God.)Tj T* (Generations later, when Saul tried to wipe out the Gibeonites)Tj T* (in his zeal for Israel, God sent a famine on Israel until David)Tj T* (made atonement \(2 Samuel 21:1-9\). The significance is)Tj T* (uncomfortable and clear: a covenant, once sworn before the)Tj T* (LORD)Tj <02>Tj (even under deception)Tj <02>Tj (is binding on the ones who)Tj T* (swore it. God takes human covenants seriously, which is one)Tj T* (reason the Bible treats covenant fidelity as sacred, not casual.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 207.7213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT -.096009 Tw 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Be careful what you swear before the LORD)Tj <03>Tj (once)Tj T* 0 Tw (made, a covenant binds you even when you were deceived.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
