istent)Tj T* (in hope. He prayed, and God answered before he finished)Tj T* (\(Daniel 9:20-23\).)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 312.5213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Confess the sins of your community as your own,)Tj T* (and pray for God's mercy on those around you.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 268.7213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 14.8 TL/F2+0 12.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 17.4 Tm (Elijah)Tj T* .545098 .396078 .031373 rg/F4+0 8.7 Tf (1 Kings 18:36-38)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 94.92126 cm .160784 .145098 .117647 rg 1.15 w BT 13.1 TL/F2+0 9.65 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 160.65 Tm (Elijah stands on Mount Carmel before a nation that has)Tj T* (wandered, and he prays a short, bold prayer that God would)Tj T* (let it be known that He is God in Israel \(1 Kings 18:36\). Fire)Tj T* (falls, the people fall on their faces, and the drought begins to)Tj T* (break. But Elijah's prayer life did not end at Carmel. After the)Tj T* (fire, he prayed again for rain, bowing down to the ground)Tj T* (with his face between his knees \(1 Kings 18:42\). And in a)Tj T* (moment of exhaustion and fear, he prayed a very different)Tj T* (prayer, asking God to take his life \(1 Kings 19:4\). God)Tj T* (answered that one too, not with fire but with a gentle whisper)Tj T* (\(1 Kings 19:12\). Elijah shows us that intercession includes)Tj T* (mountain-moving boldness and quiet, weary honesty)Tj <02>Tj (and)Tj T* (God hears both.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 66.92126 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Bring both your boldest requests and your weary)Tj T* (complaints to God, trusting Him to hear both.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
