er for others as optional, a side)Tj T* (ministry, or something to give up when people disappointed)Tj T* (him. He had already shown this pattern at Mizpah, where he)Tj T* (cried to the LORD on Israel's behalf and God answered with)Tj T* (thunder and routed the Philistines \(1 Samuel 7:5-11\).)Tj T* (Samuel's prayer life is a picture of a leader who would rather)Tj T* (be rejected by his people than fail to pray for them. His)Tj T* (mother Hannah said of him, "As long as he lives, he is lent to)Tj T* (the LORD" \(1 Samuel 1:28\), and he lived out that lending in)Tj T* (intercession.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 220.8213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Refuse to give up praying for people, even when)Tj T* (they disappoint you)Tj <03>Tj (to stop would be a sin.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
