y phrases as the Gentiles do, thinking they)Tj T* (will be heard for their many words \(Matthew 6:7\). The Lord's)Tj T* (Prayer is short, direct, and God-centered. It is a model, not a)Tj T* -.08928 Tw (formula)Tj <02>Tj (Jesus does not say "pray only these words" but "pray)Tj T* 0 Tw (then like this" \(Matthew 6:9\). And it can be prayed sincerely)Tj T* (in a minute or pondered for an hour. It teaches us that prayer)Tj T* (is not an attempt to convince a reluctant God but an approach)Tj T* (to a Father who already knows what we need before we ask)Tj T* (\(Matthew 6:8\).)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 220.8213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Pray the Lord's Prayer slowly today, pausing on)Tj T* (each phrase and letting it shape the way you pray.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
