sus, whom you anointed,)Tj T* (both Herod and Pontius Pilate, along with the Gentiles and)Tj T* (the peoples of Israel, to do whatever your hand and your plan)Tj T* (had predestined to take place \(Acts 4:24-28\). They did not)Tj T* (pray for the threats to stop)Tj <02>Tj (they prayed for boldness to keep)Tj T* (speaking. And now, Lord, look upon their threats and grant to)Tj T* (your servants to continue to speak your word with all)Tj T* (boldness \(Acts 4:29\). When they had prayed, the place in)Tj T* (which they were gathered together was shaken, and they)Tj T* (were all filled with the Holy Spirit and continued to speak the)Tj T* (word of God with boldness \(Acts 4:31\). This is the church's)Tj T* (first recorded corporate prayer for courage, and it shows us)Tj T* (that the answer to opposition is not the removal of opposition)Tj T* (but a fresh filling of the Spirit.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 168.4213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Pray not for an easy road but for boldness to keep)Tj T* (speaking Christ on the road you are on.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
