e glory of God, and Jesus standing at the right hand of)Tj T* (God \(Acts 7:55-56\). They cast him out of the city and stoned)Tj T* (him. As they were stoning him, Stephen prayed: Lord Jesus,)Tj T* (receive my spirit. And falling to his knees, he cried out with a)Tj T* (loud voice: Lord, do not hold this sin against them. And when)Tj T* (he had said this, he fell asleep \(Acts 7:59-60\). His prayer is a)Tj T* (direct echo of Jesus' own prayer on the cross)Tj <02>Tj (Lord, forgive)Tj T* (them, for they know not what they do \(Luke 23:34\). Stephen)Tj T* (is the first martyr of the church, and he died praying the way)Tj T* (Jesus died praying.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 195.5213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 27.5 Tm (Application: The next time someone wrongs you, pray for them)Tj T* (in the moment)Tj <03>Tj (that is the prayer that costs the most and does)Tj T* (the most.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
