se justified, rather)Tj T* (than the other. For everyone who exalts himself will be)Tj T* (humbled, but the one who humbles himself will be exalted)Tj T* (\(Luke 18:14\). The parable is a caution about prayer itself. The)Tj T* (Pharisee prayed)Tj <02>Tj (and it did not count. The tax collector)Tj T* -.06415 Tw (prayed)Tj <02>Tj (and it justified him. The difference was not the words)Tj T* 0 Tw (but the posture. Prayer that is a performance of our own)Tj T* (goodness is not prayer at all. Prayer that is a cry for mercy is)Tj T* (heard by God. This is the single most important lesson about)Tj T* (prayer in the Gospels: our standing before God is not built on)Tj T* (our religious record but on His mercy.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 207.7213 cm .290196 .188235 0 rg 1.15 w BT 12.2 TL/F4+0 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 15.3 Tm (Application: Start every prayer with "God, be merciful to me, a)Tj T* (sinner")Tj <03>Tj (and let that posture shape everything else you ask.)Tj T* ET Q Q Q
